BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alliance-gender-equality-strengthening-movements-2026@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260808
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alliance for Gender Equality in Europe: Strengthening Mov
 ements for Gender Equality (2026 call)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this is a gender-equality movement-building fund rather t
 han an arts or technology programme\, and it is coalition-only (no individ
 ual applicants). Relevance to creative or tech practice runs through the n
 arrative-change and digital-storytelling strand of the call. The Alliance 
 for Gender Equality in Europe\, a philanthropic initiative created in 2021
  and hosted by the Network of European Foundations\, is launching an open 
 call under its forthcoming Strengthening Movements Fund. The Alliance is c
 omposed of the Bodossaki Foundation\, Fondation BNP Paribas\, Fondation CH
 ANEL\, Fondazione con il Sud\, Fondation de France\, Fondation RAJA-Daniè
 le Marcovici\, King Baudouin Foundation and L'Oréal Fund for Women\; this
  particular fund is backed by all of those except Fondation BNP Paribas. O
 BJECTIVE: to foster collaboration and solidarity within European intersect
 ional and grassroots movements so that they can collectively advance gende
 r equality in Europe in the long term. The call follows a 2025 Alliance-co
 mmissioned mapping of European gender-equality movements (30 in-depth inte
 rviews plus contextual research) which found movements under-resourced bec
 ause philanthropic funding frameworks are misaligned with their needs\; th
 e fund is designed to replace short-term reactive funding with proactive l
 ong-term support. OUTCOMES SOUGHT: community organising reinforced at loca
 l or national level\; pan-European feminist collaborations and solidarity 
 strengthened\; alliances between gender equality and other social justice 
 movements expanded\; pro-gender-equality narratives and voices amplified i
 n local\, national\, regional or digital spaces\; policy debates informed 
 by feminist and gender equality movements. ELIGIBLE ACTIVITIES INCLUDE (no
 n-exhaustive): national\, regional or pan-European convenings and collabor
 ative projects where groups co-create joint strategies\; joint campaigns b
 etween feminist movements and allied movements (climate justice\, anti-rac
 ism\, LGBTQI+\, disability rights)\; narrative-change training for grassro
 ots groups covering framing\, messaging\, digital tools and digital storyt
 elling\; cross-border coalitions advocating EU institutions or national go
 vernments\; facilitated virtual or in-person convenings to work through in
 ternal tensions and build trust\; translating academic research on anti-ge
 nder efforts into movement strategies. ELIGIBILITY: collective proposals w
 ith at least 3 organisations per coalition (no maximum)\; legally register
 ed non-profits (NGOs\, civil society organisations\, social enterprises\, 
 national or regional funds)\; based and operating in the target countries\
 ; small and medium grassroots organisations\, defined by annual budget und
 er EUR 450\,000 (Austria\, Belgium\, Denmark\, Finland\, France\, Germany\
 , Ireland\, Luxembourg\, Netherlands\, Sweden\, UK) or under EUR 300\,000 
 (Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Bulgaria\, Croatia\, Republic of Cypru
 s\, Czechia\, Estonia\, Greece\, Hungary\, Italy\, Kosovo\, Latvia\, Lithu
 ania\, Malta\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Poland\, Portugal\, Romania\
 , Slovakia\, Slovenia\, Spain\, Serbia). Intermediary organisations and ne
 tworks are exempt from the budget thresholds but must apply in coalition w
 ith grassroots organisations\, with the budget fairly distributed among al
 l partners. Coalitions must be community-led (majority of leadership roles
  held by members of the community supported\, and/or participatory approac
 hes)\, work with marginalised women\, transgender\, non-binary and gender 
 non-conforming people\, use gender transformative approaches\, and hold an
  intersectional perspective. Proposals must be completed in English. Each 
 organisation may submit only one application\, as lead or as partner. One 
 organisation per coalition acts as lead\, is the primary contact and is le
 gally responsible for the grant\; leads are invited to networking\, peer-l
 earning and capacity-strengthening activities. SCORING (100 points): relev
 ance to the call objective 20\; demonstrated track record in strengthening
  movements 20 (learnings valued as well as achievements)\; strong impact 2
 5 (must contribute to at least one of the five outcomes\, with clear measu
 rement)\; ability to work collaboratively and inclusively with partners 20
  (including fair budget repartition)\; quality and feasibility 15. PROCESS
 : two stages. Stage 1 opened 29 June 2026 and closes 7 August 2026 at 23:5
 9 CEST\, submitted in English via the online platform (a PDF of the form i
 s downloadable for reference only). Pre-selection results by email 14 Sept
 ember 2026\; stage 2 runs 16 September to 23 October 2026 and includes due
 -diligence contact from Alliance staff\; final results by email in Decembe
 r 2026\; grants start January 2027. The Alliance is piloting a participato
 ry selection process for this call\, with grant-making decisions made join
 tly by a committee of funders and non-funders holding equal decision-makin
 g power. Q&A webinars: 6 July 2026 at 14:00 CEST and 15 July 2026 at 10:00
  CEST (registration in advance\; both have passed). An updated FAQ is publ
 ished on the call page.\n\nOrganisation: Alliance for Gender Equality in E
 urope (hosted by the Network of European Foundations)\nLocation: European 
 Union\, United Kingdom\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Kosovo\, Monte
 negro\, North Macedonia and Serbia. All coalition partners must be based a
 nd operating in these countries.\nAward: EUR 2\,700\,000 total across the 
 call. Between EUR 225\,000 and EUR 450\,000 per grant over 3 years (EUR 75
 \,000 to EUR 150\,000 per year). Project support including salary and over
 head costs\; overheads capped at 20 percent. 6 to 12 coalitions expected t
 o be funded. Free to apply.\nDuration: 3 years\, January 2027 to December 
 2029. Renewal possible at the end of the cycle subject to budget.\n\nMore:
  https://alliance-genderequality.org/call-for-proposals-strengthening-move
 ments-for-gender-equality/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://alliance-genderequality.org/call-for-proposals-strengthening-mo
 vements-for-gender-equality/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:European Union\, United Kingdom\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina
 \, Kosovo\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia and Serbia. All coalition partner
 s must be based and operating in these countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kone-foundation-annual-grant-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kone Foundation: Annual Grant Call (2026)
DESCRIPTION:Kone Foundation is Finland's major private funder for academic 
 research in the humanities\, social sciences and environmental sciences\, 
 for professional artistic work across all disciplines\, and specifically f
 or multidisciplinary projects combining scholarly and artistic approaches\
 , which is where digital culture\, media arts and artistic research propos
 als land. Individuals\, working groups and legal entities with a Finnish b
 usiness ID may apply\, and artistic groups and organisations can receive u
 p to EUR 250\,000. The Finland connection is the binding constraint: a non
 -Finnish applicant needs a Finnish institutional affiliation\, Finland res
 idence\, or the work must happen in Finland\, though international collabo
 rators can join a group freely once one member is a Finnish citizen or Fin
 land-based. Psychology\, theology\, law\, business studies without an inte
 rdisciplinary element\, and medical research are not funded\, nor are mast
 er's studies\, continuing education\, building renovation\, standalone equ
 ipment purchases or hobby activity. The annual call runs 1 to 15 September
  each year\, closing 15 September 2026 at 16:00 EEST\, with decisions anno
 unced in November and December. TIMING: funding is never retroactive and p
 rojects must begin in January or later\, so a September 2026 application f
 unds work starting January 2027 at the earliest. FLAG: Kone frames its fun
 ding around artistic work and research projects rather than festival or ev
 ent hosting as such\, so an event-led application needs to be framed as an
  artistic or research project.\n\nOrganisation: Kone Foundation / Koneen S
 aatio (Finland)\nLocation: Finland. Work may be carried out abroad by Finn
 ish citizens. Projects must have a connection to Finland.\nAward: Artistic
  groups and organisations up to EUR 250\,000\; research groups typically E
 UR 200\,000 to 500\,000. Minimum project duration six months for individua
 l applicants and one month for groups\; maximum four consecutive years for
  the same project. No co-financing requirement stated. No application fee.
  No retroactive funding.\nDuration: One month to four years\; projects mus
 t start in January or later.\n\nMore: https://koneensaatio.fi/en/grants/gr
 antapplicants/criteria-for-applying/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://koneensaatio.fi/en/grants/grantapplicants/criteria-for-applying
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finland. Work may be carried out abroad by Finnish citizens. Proje
 cts must have a connection to Finland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-irl-culture-connects-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: British Council Ireland: UK-IRL Culture Connects Grant 20
 26/27
DESCRIPTION:The UK-IRL Culture Connects Grant 2026/27 is a British Council 
 Ireland initiative delivered in association with Arts Council Ireland\, su
 pporting the early stages of artistic collaboration between Ireland and th
 e four UK nations through in-person exchange. It prioritises creative deve
 lopment over final outputs: research and development of new ideas\, mentor
 ship\, exploring collaborative pathways with producers or partners\, exper
 imenting with new technologies or practices\, and developing initiatives t
 hat support creative exchange. WHO: applications are made by individual ar
 tists or creative practitioners working as a bilateral partnership of one 
 individual based in Ireland and one based in England\, Northern Ireland\, 
 Scotland or Wales\; applicants must be resident in Ireland or the UK for t
 he project duration\, have a proven professional track record\, be at an e
 arly or developing career stage\, and not be in full-time education. One a
 pplication per collaboration. FUNDING: up to EUR 3\,000 covering artist an
 d collaborator fees\, travel and accommodation\, studio hire\, materials\,
  and access costs. Activities must involve in-person collaboration (fully 
 remote projects are not eligible) and take place between October 2026 and 
 31 March 2027. Apply via the British Council GoodGrants platform\; an info
 rmation webinar recording and overview document are on the programme page.
  DEADLINE: 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: British Council Ireland / Arts C
 ouncil Ireland\nLocation: Ireland and the UK. For bilateral partnerships o
 f one individual based in Ireland and one based in England\, Northern Irel
 and\, Scotland or Wales\; in-person collaboration required.\nAward: Up to 
 EUR 3\,000 per collaboration (smaller amounts also eligible)\, covering ar
 tist fees (including your own time)\, collaborator fees\, travel and accom
 modation\, studio or space hire\, materials\, and access costs including d
 isability support. No application fee.\nDuration: Activity between October
  2026 and March 2027\; must be completed by 31 March 2027\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.britishcouncil.ie/programmes/arts/uk-irl-culture-connects-grant-20262
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.britishcouncil.ie/programmes/arts/uk-irl-culture-connects-g
 rant-202627?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ireland and the UK. For bilateral partnerships of one individual b
 ased in Ireland and one based in England\, Northern Ireland\, Scotland or 
 Wales\; in-person collaboration required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-grounding-the-cloud-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Grounding the Cloud 2026
DESCRIPTION:Open call from the Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfon
 ds) for projects within digital culture that provide insight into and redu
 ce the ecological impact of digital technology. Data storage in the cloud\
 , generative AI chatbots and other everyday digital habits carry major eco
 logical consequences: the energy consumption of data centres\, the raw mat
 erials used for hardware\, and ever-growing e-waste. The Fund encourages p
 rojects that make the ecological (and therefore also social) impact of dig
 ital technologies and data consumption tangible\, question it\, and put al
 ternative working methods into practice\, around topics such as regenerati
 ve culture\, degrowth\, low-tech\, the reuse of obsolete hardware\, and re
 sponsibility for the technologies we use within digital culture. Applicati
 ons may concern new projects or the reinterpretation or further developmen
 t of existing initiatives that show scope for more depth or a changed appr
 oach. Collaborations in which designers\, makers or researchers engage wit
 h sustainability from an intersectional perspective are explicitly encoura
 ged. The grant may be used for artistic and substantive development\, rese
 arch\, collaboration\, knowledge sharing\, presentation and documentation.
  ELIGIBILITY: individual makers\, designers\, researchers or collectives w
 orking on alternative ways of handling digital technology\, registered wit
 h a Chamber of Commerce within the Kingdom of the Netherlands. Grant award
 s a maximum of EUR 30\,000\; maximum project duration one year. This call 
 is open from 17 August 2026\, 15:00 CEST until 14 September 2026\, 16:00 C
 EST. No application fee. Questions: digitalecultuur@stimuleringsfonds.nl.\
 n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK
 ) registration within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: Maximum EUR 
 30\,000 per grant. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; maximum 
 project duration one year.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gr
 ants/open-call-grounding-the-cloud?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-grounding-the-clou
 d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
  within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-immerse-interact-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds + Film Fund: Immerse\\Interact 2026 (se
 cond round)
DESCRIPTION:Immerse\\Interact is a joint grant scheme of the Stimuleringsfo
 nds Creatieve Industrie and the Netherlands Film Fund for immersive and in
 teractive media projects (VR\, MR\, AR and other interactive storytelling)
 . It supports artistic projects with a supporting cinematic component\, in
  which fiction or non-fiction storytelling in relation to interactive (web
 -based/mobile) or immersive technologies (XR\, room-scale projections) is 
 central. It funds both development and realisation. Development support is
  EUR 15\,000 for individual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, cappe
 d at EUR 20\,000 total) or EUR 25\,000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,00
 0 coaching)\; the coaching contribution requires a motivation from both ap
 plicant and coach plus the coach's CV\, and the development phase must res
 ult in a usable prototype. A maximum of six development contributions are 
 awarded per round\, to keep the development and realisation budgets in bal
 ance. Realisation support is up to EUR 35\,000 for individual makers or up
  to EUR 125\,000 for producers (the Fund covers a maximum of 85 percent of
  the production budget)\; note that at realisation stage the producer may 
 not also be the director\, screenwriter or designer. A separate Presentati
 on Procedure offers presentation grants for projects previously supported 
 by Immerse\\Interact after 1 January 2022. EUR 600\,000 is available per F
 und in 2026. Open to professional makers\, collectives and producers with 
 a demonstrable track record in immersive or interactive media\; applicants
  must be registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). The second 2
 026 round runs 24 June to 25 August 2026 (opens 24 June 15:00\, closes 25 
 August 16:00 CEST). No application fee. Questions: immerseinteract@stimule
 ringsfonds.nl.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie and 
 the Netherlands Film Fund\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber o
 f Commerce (KvK) registration.\nAward: Development: EUR 15\,000 for indivi
 dual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, max EUR 20\,000) or EUR 25\,
 000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching). Realisation: up to EUR
  35\,000 for individual makers or up to EUR 125\,000 for producers (Fund c
 overs max 85 percent). No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, deve
 lopment and realisation phases.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/
 en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-schem
 e?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count). The inviting foreig
 n party must cover a proportionate share of the costs. Covers hourly fees\
 , travel and accommodation directly related to the activity. IMPORTANT TIM
 ING RULE: applications are accepted from 5 months to a minimum of 7 weeks 
 before the activity begins\, and processing takes about 6 weeks. This lead
  time can rule out activities that fall shortly after a round opens. Round
  2 (4 May to 22 June 2026) has closed. Round 3 runs 8 September 2026 15:00
  CEST to 27 October 2026 16:00 CEST\, with a budget of EUR 33\,000\; given
  the 7-week rule it effectively serves activities starting from late Octob
 er 2026 onwards. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: you must already have had an appl
 ication to the Fund positively assessed within the past five years\, and a
  previous voucher does not satisfy this\, so this is not a viable first ap
 proach to the Fund. The window runs 8 September 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 27 Oc
 tober 2026\, but closes early once 20 complete applications are received. 
 Maximum one voucher per applicant per calendar year.\n\nOrganisation: Stim
 uleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation:
  Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within Eur
 ope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per trip
 \n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-voucher
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:permaculture-open-call-budejovice-2028-second-call@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: (Perma)culture Open Call 2026 (Ceske Budejovice 2028 Euro
 pean Capital of Culture)
DESCRIPTION:Second open call from Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Cu
 lture 2028\, expanding the ECoC 2028 programme. It funds cultural projects
  with an artistic or cultural output for the public in 2028\, implemented 
 in Ceske Budejovice or the South Bohemian Region\, built on regional\, nat
 ional and international cooperation. The 2026 call theme is (Perma)culture
  as a content framework (care for the Earth\, people and the future) refle
 cted through a project's process\, content and/or impact\, rather than as 
 a literal agriculture/ecology theme. All cultural and artistic fields are 
 eligible\, with extra evaluation points for: contemporary and conceptual f
 ine art (site-specific/public-space installations\, participatory and inte
 rmedia projects)\; audiovisual\, multimedia and digital arts\, immersive c
 ontent\, video game development and film (immersive AV installations\, int
 eractive digital projects\, videomapping\, VR/AR/XR\, art/educational game
 s\, digital art working with data\, AI or game principles)\; architecture\
 ; contemporary design and fashion\; contemporary music and sound art\; and
  photography. ELIGIBILITY: the 2026 call is open to legal entities (organi
 sations) with no territorial restriction (South Bohemia\, Czech Republic\,
  EU and worldwide). Individuals cannot apply but can join project teams. A
 PPLICATION: submit the application and mandatory attachments by email to o
 pencall@budejovice2028.cz (subject '(Perma)culture Open Call 2026 + [Appli
 cant Name]') and via the registration form\, plus submission via data box 
 per the call conditions. Deadline 10 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Ceske Bud
 ejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Projects implemented
  in Ceske Budejovice / South Bohemian Region\, Czech Republic\nAward: Larg
 e projects: support up to CZK 4\,000\,000 (approx. EUR 160\,000)\, min bud
 get CZK 2\,200\,000\, max 50% of total costs. Small projects: support up t
 o CZK 1\,500\,000 (approx. EUR 60\,000)\, min budget CZK 750\,000\, max 70
 % of total costs. Each project must include at least one international par
 tner and at least one South Bohemian regional partner. Budget covers two y
 ears of preparation and implementation (2027 + 2028). No application fee.\
 nDuration: Artistic/cultural output delivered for the public in 2028\; bud
 get covers preparation and implementation across 2027-2028\n\nMore: https:
 //docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdTTlZOjtEvvtKrkisZxHKecf2flkMl27a7-NeE
 kRVswjHGuQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdTTlZOjtEvvtKrkisZxHKecf2flkM
 l27a7-NeEkRVswjHGuQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Projects implemented in Ceske Budejovice / South Bohemian Region\,
  Czech Republic
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:canon-foundation-europe-research-fellowships-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Canon Foundation in Europe Research Fellowships 2026 (Eur
 ope–Japan Exchange)
DESCRIPTION:Canon Foundation in Europe Research Fellowships support bilater
 al research exchange between Europe and Japan\, awarding up to 15 fellowsh
 ips annually. AMOUNT: up to EUR 30\,000 per year (pro-rated for shorter st
 ays)\, flexible — covers living costs\, travel\, insurance\, research ex
 penses\, and books\; fellows determine their own allocation. ELIGIBILITY: 
 European nationals (including UK\, Israel\, Switzerland\, Turkey\, Balkan 
 and Baltic countries) conducting research in Japan\; or Japanese nationals
  conducting research in Europe. Applicants must have completed at least a 
 Master's or PhD degree within the last 10 years (older qualifications may 
 apply with supporting documentation). No restrictions on research field. P
 riority given to first-time applicants to Europe/Japan. Fellows arrange th
 eir own host institution and advisor. Up to 15 fellowships awarded annuall
 y. Deadline: 15 September 2026\, 23:59 CET (for fellowships starting Janua
 ry-December 2027). Apply at https://portal.canonfoundation.org/. Contact: 
 canon.foundation@canon-europe.com.\n\nOrganisation: Canon Foundation in Eu
 rope\nLocation: Europe or Japan (bilateral exchange\; fellows arrange own 
 host institution)\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000 per year (pro-rated for shorte
 r stays). No application fee.\nDuration: Minimum 3 months\, maximum 1 year
 . Fellowships for 2027 start.\n\nMore: https://portal.canonfoundation.org/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://portal.canonfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe or Japan (bilateral exchange\; fellows arrange own host ins
 titution)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rijkscultuurfondsen-interdisciplinary-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rijkscultuurfondsen: Interdisciplinary Grant
DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary grant is a new joint scheme of the six Du
 tch national cultural funds (Mondriaan Fund\, Performing Arts Fund NL\, Fu
 nd for Cultural Participation\, Netherlands Film Fund\, Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL\, and the Dutch Foundation for Literature)\, announced on 7 July
  2026. It supports makers and organisations whose work genuinely crosses t
 he boundaries of the individual funds' disciplines (visual art\, design\, 
 film\, literature\, performing arts\, and cultural participation) and cann
 ot be contained within a single discipline. TWO TRACKS: an Individual trac
 k for professional makers with a demonstrable interdisciplinary practice (
 at least one year of experience\; income cap EUR 55\,000 including the gra
 nt\; approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months)\; and an Organisation track 
 for organisations running multi-discipline projects. AMOUNT: EUR 12\,500 t
 o 50\,000 per project. ELIGIBILITY: makers and organisations based in the 
 Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. APPLYING: handled throug
 h the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal (info@mondriaanfonds.nl)\
 ; an account is required in advance. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 16:00 Dutc
 h time (single application round).\n\nOrganisation: Dutch national cultura
 l funds (Rijkscultuurfondsen)\, via the Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Netherla
 nds. For professional makers and organisations based in the Netherlands or
  the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans multiple disciplin
 es.\nAward: EUR 12\,500 to 50\,000 per project. The individual-maker track
  is approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months (income cap EUR 55\,000 includ
 ing the grant).\nDuration: Up to 12 months for the individual-maker track.
 \n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interd
 isciplinary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interdiscipli
 nary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in th
 e Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans mu
 ltiple disciplines.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
